These cookies may be set through our site by our advertising partners. They may be used by those companies to build a profile of your interests and show you relevant adverts on other sites. If you do not allow these cookies, you will experience less targeted advertising. Cookie Details List\u200e Back Button Cookie List Search Icon Filter Icon Clear checkbox label label Apply Cancel Consent Leg.Interest checkbox label label checkbox label label checkbox label label Confirm my choices"}, "https://apply.interfolio.com/187338": {"title": "Teaching Professor (Assistant or Associate) in Aerospace and Mechanical Engineering", "description": "Apply - Interfolio undefined page loaded Skip to Main Content Already have an account? Sign In Teaching Professor (Assistant or Associate) in Aerospace and Mechanical Engineering Arizona State University: Office of the University Provost: Ira A. Fulton Schools of Engineering: School for Engineering of Matter, Transport and Energy Location Tempe Campus Open Date Jun 05, 2026 Description The Ira A. Fulton Schools of Engineering at Arizona State University (ASU) and the School for Engineering of Matter, Transport and Energy ( SEMTE ) seek applicants for a position of Assistant or Associate Teaching Professor in the area of Aerospace and Mechanical Engineering. Appointment will be at the rank commensurate with the candidate\u2019s experience and accomplishments, beginning January 2027. The School for Engineering of Matter, Transport and Energy houses undergraduate and graduate programs in Aerospace, Chemical, Materials, and Mechanical Engineering. SEMTE is one of the eight schools within the Ira A. Fulton Schools of Engineering, the largest and one of the most innovative research engineering colleges in the nation. The college, which serves a large and inclusive student body, is a recognized leader in engineering education and is committed to teaching excellence. Teaching faculty members in the Aerospace Engineering and Mechanical Engineering programs are expected to develop and adopt effective pedagogical practices in the development and delivery of large-enrollment undergraduate and graduate courses in both immersion and online settings, and to mentor student projects and capstone experiences. The Ira A. Fulton Schools of Engineering supports the teaching faculty in these efforts by offering many resources through the Learning and Teaching Hub . These resources include best-practices seminars hosted by the Teaching Community of Practice , guidance for general Course Development and information about leveraging Learning Technology , among others. Additional expectations include supervising undergraduate and master\u2019s student research and projects, and undertaking service activities. Essential Functions Contribute to curriculum development Deliver instruction in-person and/or online Mentor undergraduate and/or master\u2019s students Participate in internal service Qualifications Required qualifications Earned Ph.D. in Aerospace Engineering, Mechanical Engineering or a closely related discipline by the time of appointment Evidence of excellence in teaching, as appropriate to the candidate\u2019s experience and rank Desired qualifications Technical expertise in one or more of the following areas: astronautical engineering, propulsion, orbital mechanics, and flight/space controls Commitment to delivering courses in multiple technology-enhanced formats and to curriculum development and innovative pedagogy Application Instructions Application deadline is July 31, 2026 . Applications will continue to be accepted on a rolling basis for a reserve pool. Applications in the reserve pool may then be reviewed in the order in which they were received until the position is filled. To apply, visit https://hiring.engineering.asu.edu/ and select \u201capply now\u201d next to the corresponding position. Candidates will be asked to create or use an existing Interfolio Dossier to submit the following: Cover letter clearly describing how you meet the required and desired qualifications Curriculum Vitae Statement describing teaching interests and philosophy (two pages maximum) Contact information for three references The ASU Charter states, \u201cASU is a comprehensive public research university, measured not by whom it excludes, but by whom it includes and how they succeed; advancing research and discovery of public value; and assuming fundamental responsibility for the economic, social, cultural and overall health of the communities it serves.\u201d The Ira A. Fulton Schools of Engineering is dedicated to cultivating excellence, delivering innovation that matters, encouraging bold thinking, fostering a community of learning and collaboration, and building a foundation for all to be successful. Applicants are encouraged to address how their past, current, and future activities align with the ASU Charter and Fulton Schools of Engineering values in their application materials. For additional information regarding position specifics, please contact the search committee chair, Professor James Middleton via email at jimbo@asu.edu . Application Process This institution is using Interfolio's Faculty Search to conduct\n            this search. Applicants to this position receive a free Dossier\n            account and can send all application materials, including\n            confidential letters of recommendation, free of charge. Apply Now Equal Employment Opportunity Statement A background check is required for employment. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other basis protected by law. See https://www.asu.edu/aad/manuals/acd/acd401.html and https://www.asu.edu/titleIX/ . In compliance with federal law, ASU prepares an annual report on campus security and fire safety programs and resources.\u00a0 ASU\u2019s Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available online at https://www.asu.edu/police/PDFs/ASU-Clery-Report.pdf You may request a hard copy of the report by contacting the ASU Police Department at 480-965-3456. \u00a9 2026 Elsevier Inc. or its licensors and contributors. All rights are reserved, including those for text and data mining, AI training, and similar technologies. Support | Careers | Accessibility Policy | Cookies Settings | Privacy Policy | Terms of Service We use cookies that are necessary to make our site work. We may also use additional cookies to analyze, improve, and personalize our content and your digital experience. You can manage your cookie preferences using the Cookie settings link. For more information, see our Cookie Policy Cookie settings Accept all cookies Opt-Out Request Honored Cookie Preference Center We use cookies which are necessary to make our site work. We may also use additional cookies to analyse, improve and personalise our content and your digital experience. For more information, see our Cookie Policy and the list of Google Ad-Tech Vendors . You may choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types may impact your experience of our site and the services we are able to offer. See the different category headings below to find out more or change your settings. You may also be able to exercise your privacy choices as described in our Privacy Policy Allow all Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Cookies Always active These cookies are necessary for the website to function and cannot be switched off in our systems. They are usually only set in response to actions made by you which amount to a request for services, such as setting your privacy preferences, logging in or filling in forms. You can set your browser to block or alert you about these cookies, but some parts of the site will not then work. Cookie Details List\u200e Functional Cookies Functional Cookies These cookies enable the website to provide enhanced functionality and personalisation. They may be set by us or by third party providers whose services we have added to our pages. If you do not allow these cookies then some or all of these services may not function properly. Cookie Details List\u200e Performance Cookies Performance Cookies These cookies allow us to count visits and traffic sources so we can measure and improve the performance of our site. They help us to know which pages are the most and least popular and see how visitors move around the site. Cookie Details List\u200e Targeting Cookies Targeting Cookies These cookies may be set through our site by our advertising partners. They may be used by those companies to build a profile of your interests and show you relevant adverts on other sites. If you do not allow these cookies, you will experience less targeted advertising. Cookie Details List\u200e Back Button Cookie List Search Icon Filter Icon Clear checkbox label label Apply Cancel Consent Leg.Interest checkbox label label checkbox label label checkbox label label Confirm my choices"}, "https://apply.interfolio.com/194486": {"title": "Professor (all ranks) Materials, Mechanics, and Processing for Microelectronic Packaging", "description": "Apply - Interfolio undefined page loaded Skip to Main Content Already have an account? Sign In Professor (all ranks) Materials, Mechanics, and Processing for Microelectronic Packaging Arizona State University: Office of the University Provost: Ira A. Fulton Schools of Engineering: School for Engineering of Matter, Transport and Energy Location Tempe Campus Open Date Oct 10, 2026 Description The Ira A. Fulton Schools of Engineering at Arizona State University (ASU) and the School for Engineering of Matter, Transport and Energy (SEMTE) seek applicants for a tenure-track or tenured faculty position in Materials, Mechanics, and Processing for Microelectronic Packaging. The search addresses the materials, processing, and mechanics that determine how packaged microelectronic systems are built and how they perform. We welcome candidates whose research is experimental, theoretical, or computational, and particularly encourage candidates who integrate these approaches. SEMTE ( https://semte.engineering.asu.edu/ ), one of the eight Fulton Schools, houses a vibrant mechanical, aerospace, materials, and chemical engineering research community (learn more at https://research.engineering.asu.edu/ ). We seek applicants who can enhance our abilities in these areas as part of a community of experts. Particular areas of interest include, but are not limited to: Thermomechanical reliability of advanced packages: warpage, residual stress, and die and substrate coplanarity; interfacial fracture and delamination, including at hybrid-bonded and direct-bonded interfaces; solder and interconnect fatigue; electromigration; moisture and corrosion; drop and shock survivability; materials compatibility with direct liquid and immersion cooling; and accelerated test and lifetime prediction methods. Mechanics of materials for heterogeneous integration: constitutive behavior of solders, underfills, and mold compounds, including encapsulants with tailorable thermomechanical properties; cure-, bonding-, and process-induced stress; mechanics of temporary bonding, debonding, and carriers for wafer and panel handling; and deformation and failure at small length scales and across dissimilar-material interfaces. Materials, interfaces, and processing for advanced packaging: interconnect and bonding materials; hybrid and direct bonding, thermal compression bonding, and fan-out wafer- and panel-level processes; redistribution layers, plating chemistries, and low-loss dielectrics; glass-core and organic substrates, including through-glass vias; embedded components and package-integrated passives; buried-interface chemistry and microstructure; materials for sustainable manufacturing, including non-PFAS alternatives; and wafer- and panel-level process-structure-property relationships. Characterization, metrology, and failure analysis: electron microscopy; X-ray and synchrotron methods; full-field deformation measurement; non-destructive acoustic and X-ray imaging for buried interfaces and known-good-die screening; small-scale mechanical testing; and in-situ and operando techniques. Thermal transport and thermal management for high-power-density packages: embedded cooling architectures; thermal control for 3D stacks and co-packaged optics; die-to-die thermal resistance and cross-talk; thermal isolation and spreading; thermal interface materials; and thermal and thermomechanical property measurement. Modeling, simulation, and data-driven analysis: multiscale and multiphysics modeling; constitutive model development; prediction of process-induced stress and warpage; design-for-reliability; and AI/ML methods linking metrology and test data to yield and reliability outcomes. We search for applicants who will contribute to our academic programs, promote transdisciplinary teaching and research, and help the university to achieve its aspirations, including enabling student success, transforming society, valuing entrepreneurship, and conducting use-inspired research. Faculty members in the Fulton Schools are expected to develop an internationally recognized and externally funded research program, adopt effective pedagogical practices in the development and delivery of undergraduate and graduate courses, advise both undergraduate and graduate student research and projects, and undertake service activities. ASU sits at the center of one of the fastest-growing microelectronics ecosystems in the United States. The successful candidate will have access to extensive facilities for packaging research, including ASU\u2019s MacroTechnology Works and its Advanced Electronics and Photonics Core Facility, the Eyring Materials Center, and the ASU NanoFab. These facilities support fan-out wafer-level and panel-level process development, including 300 mm wafer-level and 600 mm panel-level work carried out through SHIELD USA, a CHIPS National Advanced Packaging Manufacturing Program award led by ASU with Deca Technologies, and through the Southwest Advanced Prototyping Hub. The successful candidate will join a regional ecosystem that includes major semiconductor manufacturers, outsourced assembly and test providers, and national initiatives in microelectronics and advanced packaging. Faculty in this area are expected to engage with this ecosystem through industry collaboration and contributions to semiconductor workforce development. Appointment will be at the Assistant/Associate/(full) Professor rank, commensurate with the candidate\u2019s experience and accomplishments, beginning August 2027. Essential Functions Contribute to curriculum development. Deliver instruction in-person and/or online. Supervise honors, master\u2019s, and doctoral students. Conduct research publishable in top-tier journals and/or conferences in the discipline. Develop grant proposals for external funding as PI or co-PI. Participate in professional and internal service. Qualifications Required qualifications Earned doctorate in aerospace engineering, chemical engineering, materials science and engineering, mechanical engineering, or closely related discipline by the time of appointment. Evidence of excellence in research, as appropriate to the candidate\u2019s rank. Evidence of excellence in teaching, as appropriate to the candidate\u2019s rank. Demonstrated preparation and expertise to teach core undergraduate courses in one or more of the School\u2019s instructional areas, such as mechanics or thermal sciences. Desired qualifications Demonstrated commitment to a collaborative, transdisciplinary approach to research and teaching. Expertise in chip-package-system co-design and verification, advanced characterization, mechanical testing, or failure analysis of microelectronic materials, interconnects, or packaged structures. Interest in developing or teaching graduate coursework in microelectronics packaging, reliability, or related areas. Experience in developing or sustaining research partnerships with industry or national laboratories. Application Instructions The application deadline is November 11, 2026. Applications will continue to be accepted on a rolling basis for a reserve pool. Applications in the reserve pool may then be reviewed in the order in which they were received until the position is filled. To apply, visit https://hiring.engineering.asu.edu/ and select \u201capply now\u201d next to the corresponding position. Candidates will be asked to create or use an existing Interfolio Dossier to submit the following: Cover letter Curriculum Vitae Statement describing research interests (three pages maximum) Statement describing teaching interests and philosophy (two pages maximum) Contact information for three references The ASU Charter states, \u201cASU is a comprehensive public research university, measured not by whom it excludes, but by whom it includes and how they succeed; advancing research and discovery of public value; and assuming fundamental responsibility for the economic, social, cultural and overall health of the communities it serves.\u201d The Fulton Schools of Engineering is dedicated to cultivating excellence, delivering innovation that matters, encouraging bold thinking, fostering a community of learning and collaboration, and building a foundation for all to be successful. Applicants are encouraged to address how their past, current, and future activities align with the ASU Charter and Fulton Schools of Engineering values in their application materials. For additional information regarding position specifics, please contact the search committee chair, Jay Oswald via email at joswald1@asu.edu . Application Process This institution is using Interfolio's Faculty Search to conduct\n            this search. Applicants to this position receive a free Dossier\n            account and can send all application materials, including\n            confidential letters of recommendation, free of charge. Apply Now Equal Employment Opportunity Statement A background check is required for employment. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other basis protected by law. See https://www.asu.edu/aad/manuals/acd/acd401.html and https://www.asu.edu/titleIX/ . In compliance with federal law, ASU prepares an annual report on campus security and fire safety programs and resources.\u00a0 ASU\u2019s Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available online at https://www.asu.edu/police/PDFs/ASU-Clery-Report.pdf You may request a hard copy of the report by contacting the ASU Police Department at 480-965-3456. \u00a9 2026 Elsevier Inc. or its licensors and contributors. All rights are reserved, including those for text and data mining, AI training, and similar technologies. Support | Careers | Accessibility Policy | Cookies Settings | Privacy Policy | Terms of Service We use cookies that are necessary to make our site work. We may also use additional cookies to analyze, improve, and personalize our content and your digital experience. You can manage your cookie preferences using the Cookie settings link. For more information, see our Cookie Policy Cookie settings Accept all cookies Opt-Out Request Honored Cookie Preference Center We use cookies which are necessary to make our site work. We may also use additional cookies to analyse, improve and personalise our content and your digital experience. For more information, see our Cookie Policy and the list of Google Ad-Tech Vendors . You may choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types may impact your experience of our site and the services we are able to offer. See the different category headings below to find out more or change your settings. You may also be able to exercise your privacy choices as described in our Privacy Policy Allow all Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Cookies Always active These cookies are necessary for the website to function and cannot be switched off in our systems. They are usually only set in response to actions made by you which amount to a request for services, such as setting your privacy preferences, logging in or filling in forms. You can set your browser to block or alert you about these cookies, but some parts of the site will not then work. Cookie Details List\u200e Functional Cookies Functional Cookies These cookies enable the website to provide enhanced functionality and personalisation. They may be set by us or by third party providers whose services we have added to our pages. If you do not allow these cookies then some or all of these services may not function properly. Cookie Details List\u200e Performance Cookies Performance Cookies These cookies allow us to count visits and traffic sources so we can measure and improve the performance of our site. They help us to know which pages are the most and least popular and see how visitors move around the site. Cookie Details List\u200e Targeting Cookies Targeting Cookies These cookies may be set through our site by our advertising partners. They may be used by those companies to build a profile of your interests and show you relevant adverts on other sites. If you do not allow these cookies, you will experience less targeted advertising. Cookie Details List\u200e Back Button Cookie List Search Icon Filter Icon Clear checkbox label label Apply Cancel Consent Leg.Interest checkbox label label checkbox label label checkbox label label Confirm my choices"}, "https://apply.interfolio.com/194868": {"title": "Professor (all ranks) in Spaceflight Mechanics and Astrodynamics", "description": "Apply - Interfolio undefined page loaded Skip to Main Content Already have an account? Sign In Professor (all ranks) in Spaceflight Mechanics and Astrodynamics Arizona State University: Office of the University Provost: Ira A. Fulton Schools of Engineering: School for Engineering of Matter, Transport and Energy Location Tempe Campus Open Date Oct 12, 2026 Description The Ira A. Fulton Schools of Engineering at Arizona State University (ASU) and the School for Engineering of Matter, Transport and Energy (SEMTE) seek applicants for a tenure-track or tenured faculty position in Spaceflight Mechanics and Astrodynamics. SEMTE ( https://semte.engineering.asu.edu/ ), one of the eight Fulton Schools, houses a vibrant engineering research community (learn more at https://research.engineering.asu.edu/). We seek applicants who can enhance our abilities in these areas as part of a community of experts. Particular areas of interest include but are not limited to, Electric and Advanced Propulsion, Spacecraft Guidance, Navigation and Control (SGNC); Cislunar Astrodynamics; Satellite Constellations; Space Domain Awareness; Autonomous Systems; Orbital Debris and Space Environment; In-space Assembly, Manufacturing, and Space Robotics; and Interplanetary Trajectory and Mission Design. We search for applicants who will contribute to our academic programs, promote transdisciplinary teaching and research, and help the university to achieve its aspirations, including enabling student success, transforming society, valuing entrepreneurship, and conducting use-inspired research. Faculty members in the Fulton Schools are expected to develop an internationally recognized and externally funded research program, adopt effective pedagogical practices in the development and delivery of undergraduate and graduate courses, advise both undergraduate and graduate student research and projects, and undertake service activities. The Aerospace Engineering program, ranked by USNWR in the top 20 universities for undergraduate and the top 20 public universities for graduate programs in aerospace engineering, plans to establish new BS/MS program in Space Engineering, which provides a pathway for development of SEMTE student and faculty interaction with the space-domain research initiatives at ASU, including: the MILO Space Science Institute; the New Space Initiative; ASU-led NASA programs such as Psyche and SPARCS; and satellite fabrication facilities such as the Interplanetary Cubesat Lab. Appointment will be at the Assistant/Associate/(full) Professor rank, commensurate with the candidate\u2019s experience and accomplishments, beginning August 2027. Essential Functions Contribute to curriculum development. Deliver instruction in-person and/or online. Supervise honors, master\u2019s, and doctoral students. Conduct research publishable in top-tier journals and/or conferences in the discipline. Develop grant proposals for external funding as PI or co-PI. Participate in professional and internal service. Qualifications Required qualifications Earned doctorate in Aerospace Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, or a closely related discipline by the time of appointment. Evidence of excellence in research, as appropriate to the candidate\u2019s rank. Evidence of excellence in teaching, as appropriate to the candidate\u2019s rank. Desired qualifications Demonstrated commitment to a collaborative, transdisciplinary approach to research and teaching. Demonstrated excellence in high-quality publications in top-tier journals and/or conferences in the area of Dynamics, Controls, Spaceflight Mechanics, and Astrodynamics. Application Instructions The application deadline is November 13, 2026. Applications will continue to be accepted on a rolling basis for a reserve pool. Applications in the reserve pool may then be reviewed in the order in which they were received until the position is filled. To apply, visit https://hiring.engineering.asu.edu/ and select \u201capply now\u201d next to the corresponding position. Candidates will be asked to create or use an existing Interfolio Dossier to submit the following: Cover letter Curriculum Vitae Statement describing research interests (four pages maximum) Statement describing teaching interests and philosophy (two pages maximum) Contact information for three references The ASU Charter states, \u201cASU is a comprehensive public research university, measured not by whom it excludes, but by whom it includes and how they succeed; advancing research and discovery of public value; and assuming fundamental responsibility for the economic, social, cultural and overall health of the communities it serves.\u201d The Fulton Schools of Engineering is dedicated to cultivating excellence, delivering innovation that matters, encouraging bold thinking, fostering a community of learning and collaboration, and building a foundation for all to be successful. Applicants are encouraged to address how their past, current, and future activities align with the ASU Charter and Fulton Schools of Engineering values in their application materials. For additional information regarding position specifics, please contact the search committee chair, Matthew Peet via email at mpeet@asu.edu . Application Process This institution is using Interfolio's Faculty Search to conduct\n            this search. Applicants to this position receive a free Dossier\n            account and can send all application materials, including\n            confidential letters of recommendation, free of charge. Apply Now Equal Employment Opportunity Statement A background check is required for employment. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other basis protected by law. See https://www.asu.edu/aad/manuals/acd/acd401.html and https://www.asu.edu/titleIX/ . In compliance with federal law, ASU prepares an annual report on campus security and fire safety programs and resources.\u00a0 ASU\u2019s Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available online at https://www.asu.edu/police/PDFs/ASU-Clery-Report.pdf You may request a hard copy of the report by contacting the ASU Police Department at 480-965-3456. \u00a9 2026 Elsevier Inc. or its licensors and contributors. All rights are reserved, including those for text and data mining, AI training, and similar technologies. Support | Careers | Accessibility Policy | Cookies Settings | Privacy Policy | Terms of Service We use cookies that are necessary to make our site work. We may also use additional cookies to analyze, improve, and personalize our content and your digital experience. You can manage your cookie preferences using the Cookie settings link. For more information, see our Cookie Policy Cookie settings Accept all cookies Opt-Out Request Honored Cookie Preference Center We use cookies which are necessary to make our site work. We may also use additional cookies to analyse, improve and personalise our content and your digital experience. For more information, see our Cookie Policy and the list of Google Ad-Tech Vendors . You may choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types may impact your experience of our site and the services we are able to offer. See the different category headings below to find out more or change your settings. You may also be able to exercise your privacy choices as described in our Privacy Policy Allow all Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Cookies Always active These cookies are necessary for the website to function and cannot be switched off in our systems. They are usually only set in response to actions made by you which amount to a request for services, such as setting your privacy preferences, logging in or filling in forms. You can set your browser to block or alert you about these cookies, but some parts of the site will not then work. Cookie Details List\u200e Functional Cookies Functional Cookies These cookies enable the website to provide enhanced functionality and personalisation. They may be set by us or by third party providers whose services we have added to our pages. If you do not allow these cookies then some or all of these services may not function properly. Cookie Details List\u200e Performance Cookies Performance Cookies These cookies allow us to count visits and traffic sources so we can measure and improve the performance of our site. They help us to know which pages are the most and least popular and see how visitors move around the site. Cookie Details List\u200e Targeting Cookies Targeting Cookies These cookies may be set through our site by our advertising partners. They may be used by those companies to build a profile of your interests and show you relevant adverts on other sites. If you do not allow these cookies, you will experience less targeted advertising. Cookie Details List\u200e Back Button Cookie List Search Icon Filter Icon Clear checkbox label label Apply Cancel Consent Leg.Interest checkbox label label checkbox label label checkbox label label Confirm my choices"}, "https://apply.interfolio.com/194890": {"title": "Professor (all ranks) in Digital Engineering", "description": "Apply - Interfolio undefined page loaded Skip to Main Content Already have an account? Sign In Professor (all ranks) in Digital Engineering Arizona State University: Office of the University Provost: Ira A. Fulton Schools of Engineering: School for Engineering of Matter, Transport and Energy Location Tempe Campus Open Date Oct 13, 2026 Description The Ira A. Fulton Schools of Engineering at Arizona State University (ASU) and the School for Engineering of Matter, Transport and Energy (SEMTE) seek applicants for a tenure-track or tenured faculty position in Digital Engineering. SEMTE ( https://semte.engineering.asu.edu/ ), one of the eight Fulton Schools, houses a vibrant community of researchers spanning mechanical and aerospace engineering, chemical engineering, and materials science and engineering (learn more at https://research.engineering.asu.edu/ ). We seek applicants who can enhance our abilities in these areas as part of a community of experts. Particular areas of interest include but are not limited to, AI/ML-driven engineering; digital models, simulation, and data-driven design; autonomous and adaptive materials processing and experimentation; intelligent sensing, characterization, and control; multiscale and reduced-order modeling; virtual testing and digital engineering of structures, materials, and manufacturing processes; monitoring, prediction, and control of complex physical systems; and development of X-labs. We search for applicants who will contribute to our academic programs, promote transdisciplinary teaching and research, and help the university to achieve its aspirations, including enabling student success, transforming society, valuing entrepreneurship, and conducting use-inspired research. Faculty members in the Fulton Schools are expected to develop an internationally recognized and externally funded research program, adopt effective pedagogical practices in the development and delivery of undergraduate and graduate courses, advise both undergraduate and graduate student research and projects, and undertake service activities. At SEMTE, digital engineering is viewed as a unifying architecture that connects physical systems, computational models, sensing, data, and intelligent decision-making. In Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering (MAE), this includes modeling, simulation, sensing, data, control, and decision-making to understand, predict, and adapt the behavior of physical systems and engineering processes. Relevant directions include virtual testing and multiscale modeling of structures and materials, high-fidelity and reduced-order modeling of coupled thermal and fluid systems, digital representations of manufacturing and processing environments, diagnostics and prognostics, and intelligent sensing, planning, and control of complex engineering systems. In Materials Science and Engineering (MSE), digital engineering includes intelligent and adaptive materials processing and experimentation environments in which synthesis, characterization, modeling, data science, and AI work together to determine what experiments to run next, which parameters to explore, what information is missing, and how processing conditions should adapt as new information emerges. Research areas encompass functional, quantum, and energy materials; structural materials and biomaterials; advanced microscopy, including transmission electron microscopy; materials sustainability and lifecycle assessment; and critical materials recovery. Candidates with expertise in one or more of these areas should articulate a broader digital-engineering vision that connects their expertise to emerging AI-enabled physical systems and adaptive research environments that tightly integrate experiments, computation, sensing, and intelligent decision-making. Appointment will be at the Assistant/Associate/(f)ull Professor rank, commensurate with the candidate\u2019s experience and accomplishments, beginning August 2027. Essential Functions Contribute to curriculum development. Deliver instruction in-person and/or online. Supervise honors, master\u2019s, and doctoral students. Conduct research publishable in top-tier journals and/or conferences in the discipline. Develop grant proposals for external funding as PI or co-PI. Participate in professional and internal service. Qualifications Required qualifications Earned doctorate in Mechanical Engineering, Aerospace Engineering, Chemical Engineering, Materials Science and Engineering or closely related discipline by the time of appointment. Evidence of excellence in research, as appropriate to the candidate\u2019s rank. Evidence of excellence in teaching, as appropriate to the candidate\u2019s rank. Desired qualifications Demonstrated commitment to a collaborative, transdisciplinary approach to research and teaching. Application Instructions The application deadline is November 15, 2026. Applications will continue to be accepted on a rolling basis for a reserve pool. Applications in the reserve pool may then be reviewed in the order in which they were received until the position is filled. To apply, visit https://hiring.engineering.asu.edu/ and select \u201capply now\u201d next to the corresponding position. Candidates will be asked to create or use an existing Interfolio Dossier to submit the following: Cover letter Curriculum Vitae Statement describing research interests (Three pages maximum) Statement describing teaching interests and philosophy (two pages maximum) Contact information for three references The ASU Charter states, \u201cASU is a comprehensive public research university, measured not by whom it excludes, but by whom it includes and how they succeed; advancing research and discovery of public value; and assuming fundamental responsibility for the economic, social, cultural and overall health of the communities it serves.\u201d The Fulton Schools of Engineering is dedicated to cultivating excellence, delivering innovation that matters, encouraging bold thinking, fostering a community of learning and collaboration, and building a foundation for all to be successful. Applicants are encouraged to address how their past, current, and future activities align with the ASU Charter and Fulton Schools of Engineering values in their application materials. For additional information regarding position specifics, please contact the search committee chair, Kumar Ankit via email at kumar.ankit@asu.edu . Application Process This institution is using Interfolio's Faculty Search to conduct\n            this search. Applicants to this position receive a free Dossier\n            account and can send all application materials, including\n            confidential letters of recommendation, free of charge. Apply Now Equal Employment Opportunity Statement A background check is required for employment. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other basis protected by law. See https://www.asu.edu/aad/manuals/acd/acd401.html and https://www.asu.edu/titleIX/ . In compliance with federal law, ASU prepares an annual report on campus security and fire safety programs and resources.\u00a0 ASU\u2019s Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available online at https://www.asu.edu/police/PDFs/ASU-Clery-Report.pdf You may request a hard copy of the report by contacting the ASU Police Department at 480-965-3456. \u00a9 2026 Elsevier Inc. or its licensors and contributors. All rights are reserved, including those for text and data mining, AI training, and similar technologies. Support | Careers | Accessibility Policy | Cookies Settings | Privacy Policy | Terms of Service We use cookies that are necessary to make our site work. We may also use additional cookies to analyze, improve, and personalize our content and your digital experience. You can manage your cookie preferences using the Cookie settings link. For more information, see our Cookie Policy Cookie settings Accept all cookies Opt-Out Request Honored Cookie Preference Center We use cookies which are necessary to make our site work. We may also use additional cookies to analyse, improve and personalise our content and your digital experience. For more information, see our Cookie Policy and the list of Google Ad-Tech Vendors . You may choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types may impact your experience of our site and the services we are able to offer. See the different category headings below to find out more or change your settings. You may also be able to exercise your privacy choices as described in our Privacy Policy Allow all Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Cookies Always active These cookies are necessary for the website to function and cannot be switched off in our systems. They are usually only set in response to actions made by you which amount to a request for services, such as setting your privacy preferences, logging in or filling in forms. You can set your browser to block or alert you about these cookies, but some parts of the site will not then work. Cookie Details List\u200e Functional Cookies Functional Cookies These cookies enable the website to provide enhanced functionality and personalisation. They may be set by us or by third party providers whose services we have added to our pages. If you do not allow these cookies then some or all of these services may not function properly. Cookie Details List\u200e Performance Cookies Performance Cookies These cookies allow us to count visits and traffic sources so we can measure and improve the performance of our site. They help us to know which pages are the most and least popular and see how visitors move around the site. Cookie Details List\u200e Targeting Cookies Targeting Cookies These cookies may be set through our site by our advertising partners. They may be used by those companies to build a profile of your interests and show you relevant adverts on other sites. If you do not allow these cookies, you will experience less targeted advertising. Cookie Details List\u200e Back Button Cookie List Search Icon Filter Icon Clear checkbox label label Apply Cancel Consent Leg.Interest checkbox label label checkbox label label checkbox label label Confirm my choices"}, "https://apply.interfolio.com/194545": {"title": "Professor (all ranks) in Cement Manufacturing Science and Engineering", "description": "Apply - Interfolio undefined page loaded Skip to Main Content Already have an account? Sign In Professor (all ranks) in Cement Manufacturing Science and Engineering Arizona State University: Office of the University Provost: Ira A. Fulton Schools of Engineering: School of Sustainable Engineering and the Built Environment Location Tempe Campus Open Date Sep 28, 2026 Description The Ira A. Fulton Schools of Engineering at Arizona State University (ASU) and School of Sustainable Engineering and the Built Environment (SSEBE) seek applicants for a tenure-track or tenured faculty position in the area of cement manufacturing science and engineering. The School of Sustainable Engineering and the Built Environment (SSEBE) , one of the eight Fulton Schools, houses a vibrant infrastructural material, mechanics, manufacturing, and multi-physics modeling, simulation, and optimization research community (learn more at https://research.engineering.asu.edu/ ). We seek applicants who can complement our expertise in the broad theme of infrastructure materials, manufacturing, modeling, and performance. Particular emphasis will be given to candidates with cutting-edge research expertise advancing the next-generation of infrastructure materials manufacturing, especially, cement manufacturing and materials technologies, including process- and heat-related energy-and-emission reduction approaches to produce novel cements and cementing materials; electrification and other non-fossil energy delivery approaches for high-temperature manufacturing processes, supported by multi-scale, multi-physics modeling to accelerate the development, optimization, and scale-up of such processes; and AI- and Industry 4.0-enabled manufacturing including digital twins and data-driven optimization, with the goals of improving energy and resource efficiency, product quality, productivity, and operational resilience. We search for applicants who will contribute to our academic programs, promote transdisciplinary teaching and research, and help the university to achieve its aspirations, including enabling student success, transforming society, valuing entrepreneurship, and conducting use-inspired research. Faculty members in the Fulton Schools are expected to develop an internationally recognized and externally funded research program, adopt effective pedagogical practices in the development and delivery of undergraduate and graduate courses, advise both undergraduate and graduate student research and projects, and undertake service activities. SSEBE offers undergraduate and graduate degree programs in Civil, Environmental, Sustainable, and Construction Engineering, and in Construction Management and Technology. The school has approximately 70 faculty members, 1,500 undergraduate and 600 graduate students, and generates annual research expenditures of more than $30 million.\u00a0 Candidates will be expected to offer undergraduate and graduate courses that align with materials, processes, and sustainability related to infrastructure and the built environment. It is also expected that the candidate will enhance the capacity of existing centers and initiatives including Electrified Processes for Industrial Excellence, EPIXC, and the Center for Carbon-Efficient and Advanced Manufacturing of Materials and Structures, CAMMS. Successful candidates will support the mission of SSEBE and the Ira A. Fulton Schools of Engineering and are expected to participate in interdisciplinary research and teaching endeavors both within and beyond. Appointment will be at the Assistant, Associate or (full) Professor rank, commensurate with the candidate\u2019s experience and accomplishments, beginning August 2027. Qualifications Essential Functions Contribute to curriculum development. Deliver instruction in-person and/or online. Supervise honors, master\u2019s, and doctoral students. Conduct research publishable in top-tier journals and/or conferences in the discipline. Develop grant proposals for external funding as PI or co-PI. Participate in professional and internal service. Required qualifications Earned doctorate in civil engineering, mechanical engineering, chemical engineering, or closely related discipline by the time of appointment. Evidence of excellence in research, as appropriate to the candidate\u2019s rank. Evidence of excellence in teaching, as appropriate to the candidate\u2019s rank. Desired qualifications Demonstrated commitment to a collaborative, transdisciplinary approach to research and teaching. Professional engineering licensure or the ability to obtain registration in a timely manner. For associate and full professor candidates: Demonstrated record of securing external funding for research programs. Demonstrated record of excellence in teaching that incorporates active learning. Application Instructions The application deadline is December 15, 2026. Applications will continue to be accepted on a rolling basis for a reserve pool. Applications in the reserve pool may then be reviewed in the order in which they were received until the position is filled. To apply, visit https://hiring.engineering.asu.edu/ and select \u201capply now\u201d next to the corresponding position. Candidates will be asked to create or use an existing Interfolio Dossier to submit the following: Cover letter Curriculum Vitae Statement describing research interests (two pages maximum) Statement describing teaching interests and philosophy (two pages maximum) Contact information for three references The ASU Charter states, \u201cASU is a comprehensive public research university, measured not by whom it excludes, but by whom it includes and how they succeed; advancing research and discovery of public value; and assuming fundamental responsibility for the economic, social, cultural and overall health of the communities it serves.\u201d The Fulton Schools of Engineering is dedicated to cultivating excellence, delivering innovation that matters, encouraging bold thinking, fostering a community of learning and collaboration, and building a foundation for all to be successful. Applicants are encouraged to address how their past, current, and future activities align with the ASU Charter and Fulton Schools of Engineering values in their application materials. For additional information regarding position specifics, please contact the search committee chair, Professor Narayanan Neithalath at Narayanan.Neithalath@asu.edu . Application Process This institution is using Interfolio's Faculty Search to conduct\n            this search. Applicants to this position receive a free Dossier\n            account and can send all application materials, including\n            confidential letters of recommendation, free of charge. Apply Now Equal Employment Opportunity Statement A background check is required for employment. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other basis protected by law. See https://www.asu.edu/aad/manuals/acd/acd401.html and https://www.asu.edu/titleIX/ . In compliance with federal law, ASU prepares an annual report on campus security and fire safety programs and resources.\u00a0 ASU\u2019s Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available online at https://www.asu.edu/police/PDFs/ASU-Clery-Report.pdf You may request a hard copy of the report by contacting the ASU Police Department at 480-965-3456. \u00a9 2026 Elsevier Inc. or its licensors and contributors. All rights are reserved, including those for text and data mining, AI training, and similar technologies. Support | Careers | Accessibility Policy | Cookies Settings | Privacy Policy | Terms of Service We use cookies that are necessary to make our site work. We may also use additional cookies to analyze, improve, and personalize our content and your digital experience. You can manage your cookie preferences using the Cookie settings link. For more information, see our Cookie Policy Cookie settings Accept all cookies Opt-Out Request Honored Cookie Preference Center We use cookies which are necessary to make our site work. We may also use additional cookies to analyse, improve and personalise our content and your digital experience. For more information, see our Cookie Policy and the list of Google Ad-Tech Vendors . You may choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types may impact your experience of our site and the services we are able to offer. See the different category headings below to find out more or change your settings. You may also be able to exercise your privacy choices as described in our Privacy Policy Allow all Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Cookies Always active These cookies are necessary for the website to function and cannot be switched off in our systems. They are usually only set in response to actions made by you which amount to a request for services, such as setting your privacy preferences, logging in or filling in forms. You can set your browser to block or alert you about these cookies, but some parts of the site will not then work. Cookie Details List\u200e Functional Cookies Functional Cookies These cookies enable the website to provide enhanced functionality and personalisation. They may be set by us or by third party providers whose services we have added to our pages. If you do not allow these cookies then some or all of these services may not function properly. Cookie Details List\u200e Performance Cookies Performance Cookies These cookies allow us to count visits and traffic sources so we can measure and improve the performance of our site. They help us to know which pages are the most and least popular and see how visitors move around the site. Cookie Details List\u200e Targeting Cookies Targeting Cookies These cookies may be set through our site by our advertising partners. They may be used by those companies to build a profile of your interests and show you relevant adverts on other sites. If you do not allow these cookies, you will experience less targeted advertising. Cookie Details List\u200e Back Button Cookie List Search Icon Filter Icon Clear checkbox label label Apply Cancel Consent Leg.Interest checkbox label label checkbox label label checkbox label label Confirm my choices"}, "https://apply.interfolio.com/176193": {"title": "Professor (All Ranks): Advanced Semiconductor Packaging Focused on Co-packaged Optics", "description": "Apply - Interfolio undefined page loaded Skip to Main Content Already have an account? Sign In Professor (All Ranks): Advanced Semiconductor Packaging Focused on Co-packaged Optics Arizona State University: Office of the University Provost: Ira A. Fulton Schools of Engineering: School of Electrical, Computer and Energy Engineering Location Tempe campus Open Date Nov 03, 2025 Description The Ira A. Fulton Schools of Engineering at Arizona State University (ASU) and the School of Electrical, Computer and Energy Engineering seek applicants for a tenure-track or tenured faculty position in the area of Advanced Semiconductor Packaging. The School of Electrical, Computer and Energy Engineering, one of the eight Ira A. Fulton Schools of Engineering, houses a vibrant electrical engineering research community (learn more at https://research.engineering.asu.edu/ ). We seek applicants who can enhance our abilities in these areas as part of a community of experts. Particular areas of interest include, but are not limited to, co-packaged optics, advanced packaging/bonding to support 2.5D and 3D heterogeneous integration, package-based co-design and modeling, thermal management, power management, design for manufacturability, and package-based reliability and prognostics. We seek applicants who will contribute to our academic programs, promote transdisciplinary teaching and research, and help the university to achieve its aspirations, including enabling student success, transforming society, valuing entrepreneurship, and conducting use-inspired research. Faculty members in the Fulton Schools are expected to develop an internationally recognized and externally funded research program, adopt effective pedagogical practices in the development and delivery of undergraduate and graduate courses, advise on both undergraduate and graduate student research and projects, and undertake service activities. The School of Electrical, Computer and Energy Engineering\u2019s research areas reflect the variety of the electrical engineering profession and our faculty\u2019s expertise, ranging from the smallest nanoelectronics to the U.S. power grid and its control. Graduate students are involved in all of our research activities and have access to state-of-the-art facilities, such as the NanoFab microelectronics fabrication space on the ASU Tempe campus and the MacroTechnology Works facility, a former semiconductor plant converted to lab space. Six primary areas of specialization are control systems; electric power and energy systems; electromagnetics, antennas and microwaves; electronics and mixed-signal design; physical electronics and photonics; and signal processing and communications. In addition, new faculty hired through this search will find exciting opportunities to participate in the activities of the Southwest Advanced Prototyping (SWAP) Hub. Led by Arizona State University, the SWAP Hub is one of eight regional innovation hubs established under the Department of War\u2019s Microelectronics Commons, a national strategic initiative to accelerate the development and production of microelectronics technologies that are critical to U.S. security and defense. With over 170 partners, the SWAP Hub provides unprecedented opportunities for large-scale collaboration to advance microelectronics prototyping and lab-to-fab transition. Arizona State University is also leading the SHIELD USA project in materials and substrates for advanced packaging through the National Advanced Packaging Manufacturing Program . The recently opened Materials-to-Fab (MTF) Center, a collaboration with Applied Materials, features upgraded infrastructure to support state-of-the-art semiconductor tools, making ASU one of the few U.S. universities with access to leading-edge equipment for research, workforce development, and government-backed prototyping initiatives. The MTF Center combines Applied Materials\u2019 leadership in materials engineering with ASU\u2019s multi-disciplinary R&D expertise, creating a model that accelerates the transfer of innovations from ideation to fab prototype. Appointment will be at the a ssistant, associate, or full professor rank , commensurate with the candidate\u2019s experience and accomplishments, beginning August 2026. Essential Functions Contribute to curriculum development. Deliver instruction in-person and/or online. Supervise honors, master\u2019s, and doctoral students. Conduct research publishable in top-tier journals and/or conferences in the discipline. Develop grant proposals for external funding as PI or co-PI. Participate in professional and internal service. Qualifications Required qualifications Earned a doctorate in Electrical Engineering or a related discipline by the time of appointment. Evidence of excellence in research, as appropriate to the candidate\u2019s rank. Evidence of excellence in teaching, as appropriate to the candidate\u2019s rank. Desired qualifications Demonstrated commitment to a collaborative, transdisciplinary approach to research and teaching. Commitment to inclusive research and teaching practices. Commitment to curriculum development and innovative pedagogy. Commitment to mentoring students and delivering courses in multiple technology-enhanced formats. Record of impactful publications in top-tier journals/conferences in advanced packaging. A record of acquiring external funding. A demonstrated appreciation for entrepreneurial activities. Application Instructions The application deadline is December 31, 2025 . Applications will continue to be accepted on a rolling basis for a reserve pool. Applications in the reserve pool may then be reviewed in the order in which they were received until the position is filled. To apply, visit https://hiring.engineering.asu.edu/ and select \u201capply now\u201d next to the corresponding position.\u00a0Candidates will be asked to create or use an existing Interfolio Dossier to submit the following: Cover letter Curriculum Vitae Statement describing research interests ( two pages maximum ) Statement describing teaching interests and philosophy ( two pages maximum ) Contact information for three professional references The ASU Charter states, \u201c ASU is a comprehensive public research university, measured not by whom it excludes, but by whom it includes and how they succeed; advancing research and discovery of public value; and assuming fundamental responsibility for the economic, social, cultural and overall health of the communities it serves. \u201d The Fulton Schools of Engineering are dedicated to cultivating excellence, delivering innovation that matters, encouraging bold thinking, fostering a community of learning and collaboration, and building a foundation for all to be successful. Applicants are encouraged to address how their past, current, and future activities align with the ASU Charter and Fulton Schools of Engineering values in their application materials. For additional information regarding position specifics, please contact the search committee chair, Professor Chris Bailey, via email at Christopher.J.Bailey@asu.edu . Application Process This institution is using Interfolio's Faculty Search to conduct\n            this search. Applicants to this position receive a free Dossier\n            account and can send all application materials, including\n            confidential letters of recommendation, free of charge. Apply Now Equal Employment Opportunity Statement A background check is required for employment. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other basis protected by law. See https://www.asu.edu/aad/manuals/acd/acd401.html and https://www.asu.edu/titleIX/ . In compliance with federal law, ASU prepares an annual report on campus security and fire safety programs and resources.\u00a0 ASU\u2019s Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available online at https://www.asu.edu/police/PDFs/ASU-Clery-Report.pdf You may request a hard copy of the report by contacting the ASU Police Department at 480-965-3456. \u00a9 2026 Elsevier Inc. or its licensors and contributors. All rights are reserved, including those for text and data mining, AI training, and similar technologies. Support | Careers | Accessibility Policy | Cookies Settings | Privacy Policy | Terms of Service We use cookies that are necessary to make our site work. We may also use additional cookies to analyze, improve, and personalize our content and your digital experience. You can manage your cookie preferences using the Cookie settings link. For more information, see our Cookie Policy Cookie settings Accept all cookies Opt-Out Request Honored Cookie Preference Center We use cookies which are necessary to make our site work. We may also use additional cookies to analyse, improve and personalise our content and your digital experience. For more information, see our Cookie Policy and the list of Google Ad-Tech Vendors . You may choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types may impact your experience of our site and the services we are able to offer. See the different category headings below to find out more or change your settings. You may also be able to exercise your privacy choices as described in our Privacy Policy Allow all Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Cookies Always active These cookies are necessary for the website to function and cannot be switched off in our systems. They are usually only set in response to actions made by you which amount to a request for services, such as setting your privacy preferences, logging in or filling in forms. You can set your browser to block or alert you about these cookies, but some parts of the site will not then work. Cookie Details List\u200e Functional Cookies Functional Cookies These cookies enable the website to provide enhanced functionality and personalisation. They may be set by us or by third party providers whose services we have added to our pages. If you do not allow these cookies then some or all of these services may not function properly. Cookie Details List\u200e Performance Cookies Performance Cookies These cookies allow us to count visits and traffic sources so we can measure and improve the performance of our site. They help us to know which pages are the most and least popular and see how visitors move around the site. Cookie Details List\u200e Targeting Cookies Targeting Cookies These cookies may be set through our site by our advertising partners. They may be used by those companies to build a profile of your interests and show you relevant adverts on other sites. If you do not allow these cookies, you will experience less targeted advertising. Cookie Details List\u200e Back Button Cookie List Search Icon Filter Icon Clear checkbox label label Apply Cancel Consent Leg.Interest checkbox label label checkbox label label checkbox label label Confirm my choices"}, "https://apply.interfolio.com/193629": {"title": "Professor of Practice in Nuclear Energy and Workforce Innovation", "description": "Apply - Interfolio undefined page loaded Skip to Main Content Already have an account? Sign In Professor of Practice in Nuclear Energy and Workforce Innovation Arizona State University: Office of the University Provost: Ira A. Fulton Schools of Engineering: School of Electrical, Computer and Energy Engineering Location Tempe Campus, Polytechnic Campus, and West Campus Open Date Sep 16, 2026 Description The Ira A. Fulton Schools of Engineering at Arizona State University (ASU) seeks applicants for a Professor of Practice to accelerate education, innovation, and workforce development for the new nuclear era and preparation of the nation's engineering workforce with foundational nuclear literacy and to advance applied research in Small Modular Reactors (SMRs), digital twins, and energy systems integration, including the emerging nexus of nuclear power and data center infrastructure. This is a non-tenure track appointment with a fixed-term academic year contract and is expected to begin in August 16, 2027. The Professor of Practice will provide both strategic leadership and hands-on execution in growing ASU's nuclear energy education efforts. This individual will serve as course instructor and course portfolio director for flagship nuclear literacy offerings designed to introduce nuclear energy concepts to engineering students across all disciplines and will lead development of related micro-credential coursework. Beyond the classroom, this individual will cultivate federal agency relationships, recruit industry and utility partners, and advance ASU's SMR/data center integration research agenda. This role is designed for an experienced practitioner who remains active in the field, an individual with the credibility to engage programs at the Department of Energy (DOE), national laboratories, and with hyperscale technology companies, and the energy and disposition to subsequently engage those conversations rather than delegate. Essential Functions: Teach within the academic programs in addition to instruction of micro-credential courses with an emphasis on interdisciplinary, practitioner-informed instruction. Lead external engagement, including with federal agency relations, national laboratory partnerships (particularly Oak Ridge National Laboratory and Idaho National Laboratory), and corporate partnerships with utilities, SMR developers, and data center operators. Develop and lead joint research proposals with ASU faculty and external partners. Collaborate with ASU faculty across engineering disciplines to advance curriculum development and research cluster formation in nuclear energy and adjacent fields. Represent ASU's nuclear energy program at national conferences, federal briefings, and industry forums. Contribute to other internal services within the Fulton Schools of Engineering through committee participation, student engagement, and industry outreach. Qualifications Required Qualifications: Earned a Master's or Doctoral degree in nuclear engineering, energy systems, or a closely related discipline, plus ten (10) years of demonstrated experience in nuclear energy, advanced reactor development, federal energy policy, or national laboratory leadership, by the time of appointment. Desired Qualifications: Demonstrated experience operating at the intersection of nuclear energy and one or more of the following: federal policy, workforce development, SMR commercialization, data center or digital infrastructure energy systems, or national program leadership. Evidence of coalition-building, program development, or multi-institutional collaboration at a national scale. Effectiveness in the classroom with interdisciplinary, non-specialist audiences, particularly undergraduate and graduate engineering students outside of nuclear engineering. Established relationships with DOE, Nuclear Regulatory Commission, national laboratories, or major industry partners in the nuclear or advanced energy sector. Demonstrated ability to develop and execute, rather than merely oversee or advise. Application Instructions The application deadline is October 15, 2026 . Applications will continue to be accepted on a rolling basis for a reserve pool. Applications in the reserve pool may then be reviewed in the order in which they were received until the position is filled. To apply, visit https://hiring.engineering.asu.edu/ and select \u201capply now\u201d next to the corresponding position. Candidates will be asked to create or use an existing Interfolio Dossier to submit the following: Cover letter describing the candidate's practitioner background and vision for nuclear workforce development at national scale. Curriculum Vitae. Statement describing teaching philosophy and approach to introducing nuclear energy concepts to broad engineering audiences (two pages maximum). Contact information for three references. The ASU Charter states, \"ASU is a comprehensive public research university, measured not by whom it excludes, but by whom it includes and how they succeed; advancing research and discovery of public value; and assuming fundamental responsibility for the economic, social, cultural and overall health of the communities it serves.\" The Fulton Schools of Engineering are dedicated to cultivating excellence, delivering innovation that matters, encouraging bold thinking, fostering a community of learning and collaboration, and building a foundation for all to be successful. Applicants are encouraged to address how their past, current, and future activities align with the ASU Charter and Fulton Schools of Engineering values in their application materials. For additional information regarding position specifics, please contact Professor Keith Holbert at keith.holbert@asu.edu . Application Process This institution is using Interfolio's Faculty Search to conduct\n            this search. Applicants to this position receive a free Dossier\n            account and can send all application materials, including\n            confidential letters of recommendation, free of charge. Apply Now Equal Employment Opportunity Statement A background check is required for employment. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other basis protected by law. See https://www.asu.edu/aad/manuals/acd/acd401.html and https://www.asu.edu/titleIX/ . In compliance with federal law, ASU prepares an annual report on campus security and fire safety programs and resources.\u00a0 ASU\u2019s Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available online at https://www.asu.edu/police/PDFs/ASU-Clery-Report.pdf You may request a hard copy of the report by contacting the ASU Police Department at 480-965-3456. \u00a9 2026 Elsevier Inc. or its licensors and contributors. All rights are reserved, including those for text and data mining, AI training, and similar technologies. Support | Careers | Accessibility Policy | Cookies Settings | Privacy Policy | Terms of Service We use cookies that are necessary to make our site work. We may also use additional cookies to analyze, improve, and personalize our content and your digital experience. You can manage your cookie preferences using the Cookie settings link. For more information, see our Cookie Policy Cookie settings Accept all cookies Opt-Out Request Honored Cookie Preference Center We use cookies which are necessary to make our site work. We may also use additional cookies to analyse, improve and personalise our content and your digital experience. For more information, see our Cookie Policy and the list of Google Ad-Tech Vendors . You may choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types may impact your experience of our site and the services we are able to offer. See the different category headings below to find out more or change your settings. You may also be able to exercise your privacy choices as described in our Privacy Policy Allow all Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Cookies Always active These cookies are necessary for the website to function and cannot be switched off in our systems. They are usually only set in response to actions made by you which amount to a request for services, such as setting your privacy preferences, logging in or filling in forms. You can set your browser to block or alert you about these cookies, but some parts of the site will not then work. Cookie Details List\u200e Functional Cookies Functional Cookies These cookies enable the website to provide enhanced functionality and personalisation. They may be set by us or by third party providers whose services we have added to our pages. If you do not allow these cookies then some or all of these services may not function properly. Cookie Details List\u200e Performance Cookies Performance Cookies These cookies allow us to count visits and traffic sources so we can measure and improve the performance of our site. They help us to know which pages are the most and least popular and see how visitors move around the site. Cookie Details List\u200e Targeting Cookies Targeting Cookies These cookies may be set through our site by our advertising partners. They may be used by those companies to build a profile of your interests and show you relevant adverts on other sites. If you do not allow these cookies, you will experience less targeted advertising. Cookie Details List\u200e Back Button Cookie List Search Icon Filter Icon Clear checkbox label label Apply Cancel Consent Leg.Interest checkbox label label checkbox label label checkbox label label Confirm my choices"}, "https://apply.interfolio.com/194901": {"title": "Professor (All Ranks): Microelectronics with a Focus on Circuit/System Design", "description": "Apply - Interfolio undefined page loaded Skip to Main Content Already have an account? Sign In Professor (All Ranks): Microelectronics with a Focus on Circuit/System Design Arizona State University: Office of the University Provost: Ira A. Fulton Schools of Engineering: School of Electrical, Computer and Energy Engineering Location Tempe Campus Open Date Oct 07, 2026 Description The Ira A. Fulton Schools of Engineering at Arizona State University (ASU) and the School of Electrical, Computer and Energy Engineering seek applicants for a tenure-track or tenured faculty position in the area of microelectronics circuit/system design. The School of Electrical, Computer and Energy Engineering ( https://ecee.engineering.asu.edu/ ), one of the eight Fulton Schools of Engineering, houses a vibrant electrical engineering research community (learn more at https://research.engineering.asu.edu/ ). We seek applicants who can enhance our abilities in these areas as part of a community of experts. Particular areas of interest include, but are not limited to, design and design automation of digital/mixed-signal/communications circuits in advanced and beyond CMOS technologies; silicon photonics; design for 3D and heterogeneous integration; chip/package codesign; silicon lifecycle management; silicon realization, hardware security/trust and countermeasures. We search for applicants who will contribute to our academic programs, promote transdisciplinary teaching and research, and help the university to achieve its aspirations, including enabling student success, transforming society, valuing entrepreneurship, and conducting use-inspired research. Faculty members in the Fulton Schools are expected to develop an internationally recognized and externally funded research program, adopt effective pedagogical practices in the development and delivery of undergraduate and graduate courses, advise both undergraduate and graduate student research and projects, and undertake service activities. The School of Electrical, Computer and Energy Engineering\u2019s research areas reflect the breadth of the electrical engineering profession and our faculty\u2019s expertise, ranging from the smallest nanoelectronics to the U.S. power grid and its control. Graduate students are involved in all of our research activities and have access to state-of- the-art facilities, such as the NanoFab microelectronics fabrication space on the ASU Tempe campus and the MacroTechnology Works facility, a former semiconductor plant converted to lab and prototyping space. Six primary areas of specialization are control systems; electric power and energy systems; electromagnetics, antennas and microwaves; electronics and mixed-signal design; physical electronics and photonics; and signal processing and communications. In addition, new faculty hired through this search will find exciting opportunities to participate in the activities of the Southwest Advanced Prototyping (SWAP) Hub . Led by ASU, the SWAP Hub is one of eight regional innovation hubs established under the Department of War\u2019s Microelectronics Commons, a national strategic initiative to accelerate the development and production of microelectronics technologies that are critical to U.S. security and defense. With over 200 partners, the SWAP Hub provides unprecedented opportunities for large-scale collaboration to advance microelectronics prototyping and lab-to-fab transition. ASU is also leading the SHIELD USA project in materials and substrates for advanced packaging through the National Advanced Packaging Manufacturing Program . The Materials-to-Fab (MTF) Center, a collaboration with Applied Materials, features upgraded infrastructure to support state-of-the-art semiconductor tools, making ASU one of the few U.S. universities with access to leading-edge equipment for research, workforce development, and government-backed prototyping initiatives. MTF combines Applied Material\u2019s leadership in materials engineering with ASU\u2019s multidisciplinary R&D expertise, creating a model that accelerates the transfer of innovations from ideation to fab prototype. Appointment will be at the a ssistant, associate, or (full) professor rank , commensurate with the candidate\u2019s experience and accomplishments, beginning August 2027. Essential Functions Contribute to curriculum development. Deliver instruction in-person and/or online. Supervise honors, master\u2019s, and doctoral students. Conduct research publishable in top-tier journals and/or conferences in the discipline. Develop grant proposals for external funding as PI or co-PI. Participate in professional and internal service. Qualifications Required qualifications Earned a doctorate in Electrical Engineering or a closely related discipline by the time of appointment. Evidence of excellence in research, as appropriate to the candidate\u2019s rank. Evidence of excellence in teaching, as appropriate to the candidate\u2019s rank. Desired qualifications Demonstrated commitment to a collaborative, transdisciplinary approach to research and teaching. Record of acquiring external funding. Record of impactful publications in top-tier journals/conferences. Commitment to mentoring students and delivering courses in multiple technology-enhanced formats. Commitment to curriculum development and innovative pedagogy. A demonstrated appreciation for entrepreneurial activities. Application Instructions The application deadline is November 11, 2026. Applications will continue to be accepted on a rolling basis for a reserve pool. Applications in the reserve pool may then be reviewed in the order in which they were received until the position is filled. To apply, visit https://hiring.engineering.asu.edu/ and select \u201capply now\u201d next to the corresponding position.\u00a0Candidates will be asked to create or use an existing Interfolio Dossier to submit the following: Cover letter Curriculum Vitae Statement describing research interests ( two pages maximum ) Statement describing teaching interests and philosophy ( two pages maximum ) Contact information for three professional references The ASU Charter states, \u201c ASU is a comprehensive public research university, measured not by whom it excludes, but by whom it includes and how they succeed; advancing research and discovery of public value; and assuming fundamental responsibility for the economic, social, cultural and overall health of the communities it serves. \u201d The Fulton Schools of Engineering are dedicated to cultivating excellence, delivering innovation that matters, encouraging bold thinking, fostering a community of learning and collaboration, and building a foundation for all to be successful. Applicants are encouraged to address how their past, current, and future activities align with the ASU Charter and Fulton Schools of Engineering values in their application materials. For additional information regarding position specifics, please contact the search committee chair, Professor Krishnendu Chakrabarty at krishnendu.chakrabarty@asu.edu . Application Process This institution is using Interfolio's Faculty Search to conduct\n            this search. Applicants to this position receive a free Dossier\n            account and can send all application materials, including\n            confidential letters of recommendation, free of charge. Apply Now Equal Employment Opportunity Statement A background check is required for employment. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other basis protected by law. See https://www.asu.edu/aad/manuals/acd/acd401.html and https://www.asu.edu/titleIX/ . In compliance with federal law, ASU prepares an annual report on campus security and fire safety programs and resources.\u00a0 ASU\u2019s Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available online at https://www.asu.edu/police/PDFs/ASU-Clery-Report.pdf You may request a hard copy of the report by contacting the ASU Police Department at 480-965-3456. \u00a9 2026 Elsevier Inc. or its licensors and contributors. All rights are reserved, including those for text and data mining, AI training, and similar technologies. Support | Careers | Accessibility Policy | Cookies Settings | Privacy Policy | Terms of Service We use cookies that are necessary to make our site work. We may also use additional cookies to analyze, improve, and personalize our content and your digital experience. You can manage your cookie preferences using the Cookie settings link. For more information, see our Cookie Policy Cookie settings Accept all cookies Opt-Out Request Honored Cookie Preference Center We use cookies which are necessary to make our site work. We may also use additional cookies to analyse, improve and personalise our content and your digital experience. For more information, see our Cookie Policy and the list of Google Ad-Tech Vendors . You may choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types may impact your experience of our site and the services we are able to offer. See the different category headings below to find out more or change your settings. You may also be able to exercise your privacy choices as described in our Privacy Policy Allow all Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Cookies Always active These cookies are necessary for the website to function and cannot be switched off in our systems. They are usually only set in response to actions made by you which amount to a request for services, such as setting your privacy preferences, logging in or filling in forms. You can set your browser to block or alert you about these cookies, but some parts of the site will not then work. Cookie Details List\u200e Functional Cookies Functional Cookies These cookies enable the website to provide enhanced functionality and personalisation. They may be set by us or by third party providers whose services we have added to our pages. If you do not allow these cookies then some or all of these services may not function properly. Cookie Details List\u200e Performance Cookies Performance Cookies These cookies allow us to count visits and traffic sources so we can measure and improve the performance of our site. They help us to know which pages are the most and least popular and see how visitors move around the site. Cookie Details List\u200e Targeting Cookies Targeting Cookies These cookies may be set through our site by our advertising partners. They may be used by those companies to build a profile of your interests and show you relevant adverts on other sites. If you do not allow these cookies, you will experience less targeted advertising. Cookie Details List\u200e Back Button Cookie List Search Icon Filter Icon Clear checkbox label label Apply Cancel Consent Leg.Interest checkbox label label checkbox label label checkbox label label Confirm my choices"}, "https://apply.interfolio.com/195597": {"title": "Professor (All Ranks) in Quantum & Optical Science and Engineering", "description": "Apply - Interfolio undefined page loaded Skip to Main Content Already have an account? Sign In Professor (All Ranks) in Quantum & Optical Science and Engineering Arizona State University: Office of the University Provost: Ira A. Fulton Schools of Engineering: School of Electrical, Computer and Energy Engineering Location Tempe Campus Open Date Oct 26, 2026 Description The Ira A. Fulton Schools of Engineering at Arizona State University (ASU) and the School of Electrical, Computer and Energy Engineering seek applicants for a tenure-track or tenured faculty position in Quantum & Optical Science and Engineering. The School of Electrical, Computer and Energy Engineering ( https://ecee.engineering.asu.edu/ ), one of the eight Fulton Schools of Engineering, houses a vibrant electrical engineering research community (Learn more at https://research.engineering.asu.edu/ ). We seek applicants who can enhance our abilities in engineered quantum and photonic systems for sensing, imaging, communication, computation, and information processing. Areas of interest include, but are not limited to: quantum information theory, quantum machine learning, quantum networks, quantum communication, integrated photonics, quantum optics, quantum sensing, quantum transduction, and semiconductor-based quantum technologies. We search for applicants who will contribute to our academic programs, promote transdisciplinary teaching and research, and help the university achieve its aspirations, including enabling student success, transforming society, valuing entrepreneurship, and conducting use-inspired research. Faculty members in the Fulton Schools of Engineering are expected to develop an internationally recognized and externally funded research program, adopt effective pedagogical practices in the development and delivery of undergraduate and graduate courses, advise both undergraduate and graduate student research and projects, and undertake service activities. The School of Electrical, Computer and Energy Engineering\u2019s research areas reflect the breadth of the electrical engineering profession and our faculty\u2019s expertise, ranging from the smallest nanoelectronics, to the U.S. power grid and its control. Graduate students are involved in all of our research activities and have access to state-of- the-art facilities, such as the NanoFab microelectronics fabrication space on the ASU Tempe campus and the MacroTechnology Works facility, a former semiconductor plant converted to lab and prototyping space. Six primary areas of specialization are control systems; electric power and energy systems; electromagnetics, antennas and microwaves; electronics and mixed-signal design; physical electronics and photonics; and signal processing and communications. In addition, new faculty hired through this search will find exciting opportunities to participate in the activities of the Southwest Advanced Prototyping (SWAP) Hub . Led by Arizona State University, the SWAP Hub is one of eight regional innovation hubs established under the Department of War\u2019s Microelectronics Commons, a national strategic initiative to accelerate the development and production of microelectronics technologies that are critical to U.S. security and defense. With over 200 partners, the SWAP Hub provides unprecedented opportunities for large-scale collaboration to advance microelectronics prototyping and lab-to-fab transition. Arizona State University is also leading the SHIELD USA project in materials and substrates for advanced packaging through the National Advanced Packaging Manufacturing Program . The Materials-to-Fab (MTF) Center, a collaboration with Applied Materials, features upgraded infrastructure to support state-of-the-art semiconductor tools, making ASU one of the few U.S. universities with access to leading-edge equipment for research, workforce development, and government-backed prototyping initiatives. MTF combines Applied Materials\u2019 leadership in materials engineering with ASU\u2019s multidisciplinary R&D expertise, creating a model that accelerates the transfer of innovations from ideation to fab prototype. Appointment will be at the Assistant, Associate, or (full) Professor rank commensurate with the candidate\u2019s experience and accomplishments, beginning August 2027. Essential Functions Contribute to curriculum development. Deliver instruction in-person and/or online. Supervise honors, master\u2019s, and doctoral students. Conduct research publishable in top-tier journals and/or conferences in the discipline. Develop grant proposals for external funding as PI or co-PI. Participate in professional and internal service. Qualifications Required qualifications Earned a doctorate in electrical engineering or a closely related discipline by the time of appointment. Evidence of excellence in research, as appropriate to the candidate\u2019s rank. Evidence of excellence in teaching, as appropriate to the candidate\u2019s rank. Desired qualifications Demonstrated commitment to a collaborative, transdisciplinary approach to research and teaching. Record of impactful publications in top-tier journals/conferences. Application Instructions The application deadline is November 30, 2026 . Applications will continue to be accepted on a rolling basis for a reserve pool. Applications in the reserve pool may then be reviewed in the order in which they were received until the position is filled. To apply, visit https://hiring.engineering.asu.edu/ and select \u201capply now\u201d next to the corresponding position. Candidates will be asked to create or use an existing Interfolio Dossier to submit the following: Cover letter Curriculum Vitae Statement describing research interests ( two pages maximum ) Statement describing teaching interests and philosophy ( two pages maximum ) Contact information for three references The ASU Charter states, \u201c ASU is a comprehensive public research university, measured not by whom it excludes, but by whom it includes and how they succeed; advancing research and discovery of public value; and assuming fundamental responsibility for the economic, social, cultural and overall health of the communities it serves. \u201d The Fulton Schools of Engineering is dedicated to cultivating excellence, delivering innovation that matters, encouraging bold thinking, fostering a community of learning and collaboration, and building a foundation for all to be successful. Applicants are encouraged to address how their past, current, and future activities align with the ASU Charter and Fulton Schools of Engineering values in their application materials. For additional information regarding position specifics, please contact the search committee chair, Professor Christian Arenz, at Christian.Arenz@asu.edu . Application Process This institution is using Interfolio's Faculty Search to conduct\n            this search. Applicants to this position receive a free Dossier\n            account and can send all application materials, including\n            confidential letters of recommendation, free of charge. Apply Now Equal Employment Opportunity Statement A background check is required for employment. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other basis protected by law. See https://www.asu.edu/aad/manuals/acd/acd401.html and https://www.asu.edu/titleIX/ . In compliance with federal law, ASU prepares an annual report on campus security and fire safety programs and resources.\u00a0 ASU\u2019s Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available online at https://www.asu.edu/police/PDFs/ASU-Clery-Report.pdf 